# Twisted automorphic descents: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It records which of
its headline theorems can be stated against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs.
None can be stated on those APIs using only a few simple definitions.

The following headline theorems are not statable at the pins:
- Section 1.3, First-occurrence cuspidality: lacks actual cuspidal automorphic realizations, rational Bessel images and their Hilbert topology.
- Section 1.4, Multiplicity-free Bessel decomposition: lacks actual cuspidal automorphic realizations, rational Bessel images and their Hilbert topology.
- Section 2.2, Bessel functional factorization: lacks rational classical Bessel data, normalized induced automorphic representations and Eisenstein families.
- Section 2.3, Relative Bruhat cells: lacks rational classical Bessel data, normalized induced automorphic representations and Eisenstein families.
- Section 2.4, Open-cell reduction: lacks rational classical Bessel data, normalized induced automorphic representations and Eisenstein families.
- Section 3.2, Euler product of the zeta integral: lacks continuous local Bessel models and classical-group local zeta integrals.
- Section 3.4, Unramified Bessel integral calculation: lacks continuous local Bessel models and classical-group local zeta integrals.
- Section 3.6, Open-cell local nonvanishing: lacks continuous local Bessel models and classical-group local zeta integrals.
- Section 4.3, Maximal pole and central L-value: lacks completed automorphic parameter L-functions and continuous Eisenstein Laurent operators.
- Section 4.5, Holomorphy at the critical point: lacks completed automorphic parameter L-functions and continuous Eisenstein Laurent operators.
- Section 4.6, Reciprocal nonvanishing of Bessel periods: lacks completed automorphic parameter L-functions and continuous Eisenstein Laurent operators.
- Section 4.7, Nonzero period implies nonzero central value: lacks completed automorphic parameter L-functions and continuous Eisenstein Laurent operators.
- Section 5.2, Residual square integrability and packet membership: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 5.4, Vanishing above the critical index: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 5.5, Cuspidality at the critical index: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 5.6, Outer stability of critical Bessel modules: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 5.7, Unramified parameter of the critical module: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 5.8, Structure of the critical cuspidal module: lacks classical Arthur packets, residual automorphic modules and twisted Jacquet realizations.
- Section 6.3, Known Fourier-support cases: lacks rational Fourier support on residual packets and coherent automorphic period carriers.
- Section 6.4, Central value produces a global period: lacks rational Fourier support on residual packets and coherent automorphic period carriers.
- Section 6.5, Odd orthogonal–torus period criterion: lacks rational Fourier support on residual packets and coherent automorphic period carriers.
- Section 7.2, Cuspidal module recovery theorem: lacks actual twisted descent modules, enhanced local packets and cuspidal automorphic realizations.
- Section 7.3, Recovery from a regular Fourier coefficient: lacks actual twisted descent modules, enhanced local packets and cuspidal automorphic realizations.
- Section 7.4, Generic summand from subregular support: lacks actual twisted descent modules, enhanced local packets and cuspidal automorphic realizations.
- Section 7.5, Recovery from subregular support: lacks actual twisted descent modules, enhanced local packets and cuspidal automorphic realizations.

The shifted tempered-factor comparison of Section 3.5 also lacks the actual
standard modules and all-place signed Asai factors. Its general factor and
unitary-dual theorems belong to the named suppliers.

Native partitions, matrix representations and meromorphic functions alone do
not carry these objects. Arithmetic partition-size identities, scalar period
identities and boundary computations are README Checks, not substitute
headlines. No conjectural condition is represented by an arbitrary predicate,
and no missing construction is encoded as admitted data.
